h2: complete an empty request body for every method, not just POST

An h2 request without Content-Length whose END_STREAM came on the HEADERS
has an empty, complete body: lws_http_action() already marks it
content_length_explicitly_zero.  But the empty LWS_CALLBACK_HTTP_BODY and
LWS_CALLBACK_HTTP_BODY_COMPLETION are only raised for a POST; a PUT,
PATCH, DELETE or OPTIONS goes straight to no_more_body with no callback.

An application reading the request body of an h2 request without
Content-Length (DATA frames up to END_STREAM) cannot tell an empty body
from one still to come, since no public API says END_STREAM arrived with
the HEADERS, so it waits for a completion that never comes and the
request hangs.  A PUT or PATCH has a body as much as a POST (the cgi
branch just above already ends stdin whatever the method).

Raise them for any request on an h2 / h3 stream (mux_substream).  h1 is
unchanged: an h1 request with no framing has no body and nothing waits
for one.  The "already answered" check below still applies, so an app
that completed the transaction from LWS_CALLBACK_HTTP is not called.

Not an upstream backport: v5.1.0 (5f39aa483) and main (d954e68f2) both
gate on method_post.

